  misleads a reader, all of which cost time on that run:

    1. The layer panels are a horizontal PAGER. The previously selected panel is parked off
       the left edge at a negative x and WDA still calls it visible="true".
    2. The brightness sub-panel is a pager nested inside a pager, and iOS gives its children
       the enclosing cell's ORIGIN with their own size. `Brightest-Darkest` reports
       (0, 202, 108, 17) while rendering near the bottom of the form, and WDA agrees it is not
       displayed. Its bogus midpoint lands on the `Select IC Continuously` row, which is
       included here at its real rect: asking for Brightness Order opened Select Type.
    3. The Workshop list is a grid whose caption sits BELOW its tile, so a tile's edit badge
       is above its own label and below the label of the tile in the row above.
    4. Section fold buttons all share one name, so they can only be told apart by which
       header they sit level with.
-->
